id: rust.mutex
kind: rust
title: Mutex (std and tokio)
aliases: mutex, lock, critical section
tags: concurrency, sync
questions:
  - what is the difference between std::sync::Mutex and tokio::sync::Mutex?
invariant: A mutex serializes access to the value it guards, so contention on a hot lock serializes unrelated work; which mutex you choose must match whether the critical section may await.
answer_30s: std::sync::Mutex blocks the OS thread and suits short non-async critical sections; tokio::sync::Mutex is awaitable and is for guards held across an await.
answer_2m: |
  Locking a std Mutex in async code is fine as long as the guard never crosses
  an await: otherwise you block a runtime worker thread, and the guard is not
  Send so the future cannot be spawned. A tokio Mutex parks the task instead of
  the thread, at a higher cost per acquisition. The high-value discipline is to
  shrink the critical section: read or clone the minimum value out, release,
  then do the slow work outside the lock. That discipline, plus read-mostly
  RwLock or message passing, is what keeps a mutex from becoming the bottleneck
  that autoscaling cannot fix.
when_to_use:
  - guarding a small state transition that several tasks must serialize
avoid_when:
  - guarding a whole request path, a connection pool, or anything with slow work inside the lock
minimal_example: |
  use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

  let hits = Arc::new(Mutex::new(0u64));
  { let mut h = hits.lock().unwrap(); *h += 1; } // critical section only

  // async variant, needed only when the guard crosses an await:
  let m = tokio::sync::Mutex::new(0u64);
  let _g = m.lock().await;
failure_modes:
  - holding a std MutexGuard across .await
  - lock contention creating a bottleneck autoscaling cannot fix
  - poison: a panicking thread poisons the lock so later lock().unwrap() panics too
misuse:
  - tokio mutex for everything => pays async overhead for guards that never await
follow_ups:
  - how do you avoid contention on a hot path?
related:
  - rust.rwlock
  - rust.raii
  - rust.arc
  - rust.mutex-across-await
  - rust.atomics
  - design.shared-state
sources:
  - https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html
  - https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/sync/struct.Mutex.html
